### Page 3 of 11

```text
Annexation/UDC-15-00814/BRDN
3
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:

This annexation application is for about one acre (43,770 square feet) of land northeast of the
intersection of Dell Range Boulevard and Gysel Place. This application was submitted along with a zone
change application. The land to be annexed will need to be given a City zone. The zone change
application proposes changing the County AR Agricultural Residential zone to MUB Mixed-Use Business
Emphasis.

PlanCheyenne is supportive of annexing this land into the City. This land is located within the Urban
Service Boundary and is designated in the future land use plan as Urban Residential. Residential zoning is
recommended for Urban Residential designated areas by PlanCheyenne.

City services will provide environmental quality benefits to both the current residents and future
residents. As with any expansion there will be an impact on service provision within the City. However, as
this is a small expansion adjacent to current City Services, the impact on City services will be minor.

With this annexation and subsequent development, it is expected that the area will be developed
according to standards of the Unified Development Code (UDC). It is also expected that all utilities will be
stubbed to the edges of the project to allow future development on neighboring properties to occur.
Undeveloped land to the north and east is anticipated to develop as Urban Residential and Urban
Transitional Residential by PlanCheyenne.

Due to meeting the review criteria found in Wyoming Statute 15-1-402, staff recommends
approval of this annexation, with conditions.
```

