### Page 6 of 11

```text
Annexation/UDC-15-00814/BRDN
6

PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan.

This annexation is consistent with PlanCheyenne.

PlanCheyenne calls for development within the
Urban Service Boundary, which this plat is. On the
future land use map found in PlanCheyenne, the
subject area has been designated as Urban
Residential. The land to the north and east is
designated Urban Residential and Urban
Transitional Residential. The Urban Residential
land use designation is for a broad variety of
housing types and densities. Urban Residential
also contemplates complimentary uses being
integrated within the neighborhoods to serve the
community. Urban Residential type development
is best served by being inside the City limits with
access to City services. PlanCheyenne
recommends residential zones for Urban
Residential areas.

Braden Homesites is near proposed recreation
facilities in PlanCheyenne. These recreation features
 will serve this neighborhood once they are constructed.

ANNEXATION ELIGIBILITY DATA/ANALYSIS: Before any territory is eligible for annexation, the
governing body must find that the following criteria are met (W.S. § 15-1-402 (a)):

COMMON WELFARE – An annexation of the area is for the protection of the health, safety, and welfare of
the persons residing in the area and in the city or town.

The annexation of this property will increase the health, safety, and welfare of the residents of
the development once it is built. By being in City limits, the residential will receive access to City
Fire and Police services. The residents will also be connected to City Water and Sanitary Sewer
instead of having wells and septic systems.

PART OF THE CITY – The urban development of the area sought to be annexed would be constituted a
natural, geographic, economic, and social part of the annexing city or town.

This property, once developed, will constitute a natural, geographic, economic, and social part of
the city. The contiguity to the south and the location along a major arterial makes the parcel a
natural geographic part of the City. The residents will likely work in the Cheyenne area and will
be a part of the social and economic fabric that is Cheyenne.

Map #3 – Zone Districts
Source: Cheyenne/Laramie County GIS
Cooperative Program
```

### Page 7 of 11

```text
Annexation/UDC-15-00814/BRDN
7

LOGICAL EXPANSION – The area sought to be annexed is a
logical and feasible addition to the annexing city or town and
the extension of basic and other services customarily available
to residents of the city or town shall, within reason, be
available to the area proposed to be annexed.

The area is a logical and feasible addition to the City
due to the reasons previously listed. All City services
normally available to residents will also be available
to this location.  As with any expansion at the edge of
the City the expansion will require the expansion of
City services.

CONTIGUOUS – The area sought to be annexed is contiguous
with or adjacent to the annexing city or town, or the area
meets the requirements of W.S. 15-1-407.

The parcels proposed for annexation is about 31%
contiguous, all along the southern edge of the
parcels.

UTILITIES – If the city or town does not own or operate its own electric utility, its governing body is
prepared to issue one (1) or more franchises as necessary to service the annexed area pursuant to W.S.
15-1-4102.

Utility franchises are in place to serve the parcels.

CERTIFIED MAILING – The annexing city or town, not less than twenty (20) business days prior to the
public hearing required by W.S. 15-1-405(a), has sent by certified mail to all landowners and affected
public utilities within the territory a summary of the proposed annexation report as required under
subsection (c) of this section and notice of the time, date, and location of the public hearing required by
W.S. 15-1-405(a).

A certified mailing was made to the required agencies on January 8, 2016.

ANNEXATION REPORT DATA: In compliance with W.S. § 15-1-402(c) the following information is
provided:
(i)
A map is not required for this report based on the absence of exercising the authority
granted under W.S. 15-3-202 (b) (ii).
(ii)
The total estimated cost of infrastructure improvements required of the landowners by the
City related to the annexation is approximately $48,000.00.  Estimated costs include the
extension of the sewer main and connection of existing structures to the sewer. Additional
on- and off-site improvements may be required with subsequent development actions.
(iii)
Services customarily available to City residents include water, sewer, sanitation, police and
fire protection. Police and Fire services will be provided immediately upon the recording of
the annexation. Water and sewer services are provided upon application and payment to the
Board of Public Utilities, with sanitation services occurring concurrently. Provision of these
services is initiated by the property owner. Development will require extension of water and
sewer services, which are available to the subject property.
Map #4 – Current City Boundaries
Source: Cheyenne/Laramie County GIS
Cooperative Program
